From 4900e605f85a4658270b292c1919299d599586da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:35:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Windows (MinGW clang / Zig) build of the Vulkan backend

- rsx_vulkan_backend.c: no longer Linux-only. Its POSIX calls (dlopen,
  pthread mutexes, clock_gettime) go through small backend-local wrappers:
  LoadLibrary(vulkan-1.dll), SRW locks and the performance counter on Win32.
- CMakeLists: PS3RECOMP_RSX_VULKAN allowed on Windows; there it links SDL2
  (window) and selects the SDL2 pad and audio backends, so input (keyboard
  included) and audio match Linux. glslang is looked up whenever Vulkan is on.
- cellPad: the SDL keyboard fallback is compiled with the SDL2 backend on
  any platform.
- rsx_shader_spirv: the translation cache key is a hash of the translator's
  source and header (passed by CMake) instead of __DATE__/__TIME__, which
  Zig rejects and which made builds unreproducible. Its COMPILE_DEFINITIONS
  are appended, not replaced.
- ppu_loader: builds with clang in MinGW mode (no SEH: the stack sampler
  bounds its reads with VirtualQuery; a forward declaration matched to its
  static definition).
